.TH "CSDLC-INSTALL" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-install \- validate or execute an issue\-bound binary installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc install \-\-request REQUEST
\&csdlc install \-\-help
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Validates source provenance, selected binary and selector metadata digests plus stable destination. Executes only when install.executes_install is true, current bound issue ownership validates, and explicit exact\-head cutover approval proof matches. Executing destination is exactly .adl/bin/csdlc in the bound checkout. This is separate from adl/tools/install_owner_binaries.sh, which installs operational owners and man pages to .adl/bin/native\-v3.
.SH OPTIONS
\&\-\-request: Required path to a UTF\-8 JSON request of the command's request family.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.SH REQUEST
\&ProofRouteRequest and its typed binding/manifest/install fields are described in csdlc\-requests(1). Paths must stay within the authenticated bound issue evidence boundary; they are not arbitrary shell execution or filesystem destinations.
.SH EFFECTS
\&Preview checks; admitted executing install copies the verified binary, sets executable permissions and retains receipt. A validated install plan alone performs no deployment.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&csdlc install \-\-request install\-request.json
.fi
.PP
\&Fixture examples are parse\-checked; historical shadow/soak examples intentionally exercise their blocked behavior. Proof/install require actual current binding and valid referenced artifacts for success.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
\&Blocked reports use schema csdlc.v3.proof_route.v1 on stdout and a short stderr message with exit 2. Missing/stale binding, path escape, artifact digest mismatch and unauthorized execution remain blockers. Inspect status and findings before calling a proof complete.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1).
